  "copy": {
    "series_title": "The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026",
    "caption": "Like Blech.Brut, Atelier VRAI are among my personal NEIPA heroes. I love their beers and order almost every new release, so I’m especially happy to see them in this year’s festival line-up.\n\nAtelier VRAI is next in The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026.\n\nTheir story began in 2016, when Nico Döring founded Atelier der Braukünste, the company now known as Atelier VRAI. The starting point was a small nano-brewing system at Romrod Castle in Hesse.\n\nMeet Atelier VRAI at the Trier Beer Festival on 2–3 October 2026 at Blesius Garten, Trier, hosted by @kraft_braeu_trier and @blesius_garten.\n\nExplore their story on Beer Chronicles through the link in the accompanying Story.\n\nTickets are still available:\nhttps://www.ticket-regional.de/events_info.php?eventID=275224\n\n#BeerChronicles #TrierBeerFestival #AtelierVRAI #BeerHistory #NEIPA",
    "story_text": "BEER CHRONICLES\nThe Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026\nAtelier VRAI\n2016\nAtelier VRAI begins as Atelier der Braukünste.\nTRIER BEER FESTIVAL · 2–3 OCTOBER 2026 · BLESIUS GARTEN\nTickets still available — see feed caption\nbeer-chronicles.org",
    "alt_text": "Cream poster with centred charcoal serif lettering and fine copper rules. At the top: “BEER CHRONICLES” and “The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026”. The original Atelier VRAI logo shows a small sketched bird above the words “ATELIER VRAI”, on its retained white background. Below: “2016” in copper and “Atelier VRAI begins as Atelier der Braukünste.” The footer reads “TRIER BEER FESTIVAL · 2–3 OCTOBER 2026 · BLESIUS GARTEN”, followed by “beer-chronicles.org”."
  },
